{{also|Machen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|-}}, from {{inh|de|goh|mahhōn}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*makōną}}; akin to {{cog|nds|maken}}, {{cog|nl|maken}}, {{cog|en|make}}, {{cog|fy|meitsje}}. Ultimately from {{der|de|ine-pro|*mag-|t=to knead, mix, make}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmaxən/|[ˈmaχ(ə)n]|[ˈmäxən̩]|['mäxɛn]|['mɑχən]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-machen.ogg|audio (Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-machen.ogg|audio (Austria and Southern Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aχn|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-weak|macht|machte|gemacht}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[make]]; to [[produce]]; to [[create]] an object, arrangement, situation etc.
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''hab''' dir einen Kuchen '''gemacht'''!|inline=1|I '''have made''' you a pie!}}
#: {{ux|de|Du hast einen Fehler '''gemacht'''.|inline=1|You '''made''' a mistake.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[take]] (a [[photo]])
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[prepare]] {{qualifier|e.g. food, drinks}}
#: {{ux|de|'''Machst''' du heute das Essen?|inline=1|'''Will''' you '''prepare''' dinner today?}}
#: {{ux|de|sich eine Pizza '''machen'''|inline=1|to heat up or make a pizza for oneself}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|informal}} to [[do]] {{qualifier|to perform an action}}
#: {{ux|de|'''Mach''' es!|inline=1|'''Do''' it!}}
#: {{ux|de|Das '''hat''' er ganz allein '''gemacht'''!|inline=1|He '''has done''' that all by himself!}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|colloquial}} to [[matter]] (only [[impersonally]])
#: {{ux|de|Das '''macht''' nichts!|inline=1|That doesn't '''matter'''!}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|informal|colloquial}} to [[come to]]; to [[total]]; to [[cost]] {{qualifier|prizes}}
#: {{ux|de|Wie viel '''macht''' das?|inline=1|How much '''does''' that '''come to'''?}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|informal|colloquial}} to [[earn]]; to receive or create [[profit]]
#: {{ux|de|Der Herr Müller ist echt reich; der '''macht''' mehr als 5000 im Monat.|inline=1|Mr Müller is quite rich; he '''makes''' more than 5000 bucks per month.}}

====Usage notes====
Unlike English, the verb {{m|de|machen|t=[[make]]}} is used as a synonym for {{m|de|tun|t=[[do]]}} in most cases. However, ''tun'' cannot be used for the proper senses of ''machen''.

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj-weak|mach|gemacht|h}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to make, to produce}} {{l|de|produzieren}}, {{l|de|herstellen}}
* {{sense|to do}} {{l|de|tun}}
* {{sense|to prepare food, drinks}} {{l|de|vorbereiten}}
* {{sense|to matter}} {{l|de|eine Rolle spielen}}, {{l|de|wichtig sein}}
* {{sense|to come to, to total, to cost}} {{l|de|kosten}}
* {{sense|to earn}} {{l|de|verdienen}}, {{l|de|einheimsen}}

